<div class="container">

<header class="main-header">
  <div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Orach Chaim</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Tisha B&rsquo;Av v&rsquo;Ta&rsquo;aniyos</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Halacha 4</div>
  <div class="halacha-num">26 Oaseyos</div>
  <div class="source-ref-header">Based on the Torah &ldquo;Chadei Rabbi Shim&rsquo;on&rdquo;<br>see there in siman 61; and there it is explained that through<br>the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> [faith in the Sages],<br>foul smokes [<span class="heb-term">ashanos s&rsquo;ruchim</span>] rise up, etc.<br>And through this, one&rsquo;s counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] is divided, etc.</div>
</header>

<!-- OAS 1 -->
<div class="section-marker">1</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the main point of the distress [<span class="heb-term">tzarah</span>] of the <span class="concept">Churban of the Bais HaMikdash</span> and the <span class="concept">Galus</span> [exile] of Yisrael from their land &mdash; it was all through the <span class="concept">damage to emunas Chachamim</span> [faith in the Sages], as is written. And they were mockers [<span class="heb-term">mal&rsquo;igim</span>] of the <span class="heb-term">malach&rsquo;ay ha&rsquo;Elokim</span> [messengers of G-d] (and as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said in Maseches Shabbas: &ldquo;and from then there is for us no counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>]&rdquo;; as is written, &ldquo;counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] has been lost from the wise [<span class="heb-term">banim</span>],&rdquo; etc. And this is &mdash; counsel was lost from the wise &mdash; their wisdom was taken away &mdash; meaning, through foul smokes [<span class="heb-term">ashanos s&rsquo;ruchim</span>] that confuse the wisdom &mdash; in the aspect of &ldquo;their wisdom was taken away&rdquo; &mdash; through this, counsel was lost from the wise, etc., as above. And about this, Dovid HaMelech cried out, &ldquo;until when will I place counsels [<span class="heb-term">aitzos</span>] in my soul,&rdquo; etc.) &mdash; this is stated about the <span class="concept">four exiles</span> [<span class="heb-term">arba galyuyos</span>], as Rashi explains there, that the main point of the distress is that one cannot place counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] in his soul about what he needs.</p>

<p>For a person needs much counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] in this world all the days of his life, in order to be able to save himself from that which he needs &mdash; to be saved so as not to lose both worlds, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>. For whoever has brains [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>], in his holy [<span class="heb-term">kodshai k&rsquo;dashav</span>] &mdash; it is fitting for him to place his heart upon his matters &mdash; what is happening with him in this world, and for what reason he came to this world &mdash; to pass through in worry and distress and suffering and anger and pains, as if the end [<span class="heb-term">sof</span>] of everything is dust and ashes, worms and maggots! And who knows how his judgment and sentence will come out on the Great and Awesome Day of Judgment &mdash; for it is great and awesome indeed, as is written: awesome and fearful is He, and who can contain it!</p>

<p>Certainly every person needs to take stock of [<span class="heb-term">l&rsquo;fakei&rsquo;ach</span>] his dealings and to place counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzos</span>] in his soul &mdash; perhaps he can save his soul. And the main thing is <span class="concept">true counsel</span> [<span class="heb-term">aitzos amitiyos</span>]. For the main purpose of all wisdom is counsel &mdash; for certainly this is no wisdom, to make schemes of robbery &mdash; a wondrous marvel [<span class="heb-term">nifla&rsquo;ah</span>] in great wisdom. And afterward it is by itself destroyed through his hand, as one who has already committed many evils of this sort &mdash; as is explained (and as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said: &ldquo;gradually, gradually, it will be written [<span class="heb-term">Sadna b&rsquo;Sadnaih yaseiv</span>]&rdquo;). (And see this below in Hilchos Sukkah.) And certainly the main purpose of wisdom is &mdash; when one succeeds through the brilliance [<span class="heb-term">ziv</span>] of the wisdom &mdash; meaning, when counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] comes out of the wisdom that succeeds through his hand. But also when one succeeds in this world through the wisdom &mdash; still, this is not true complete counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah sh&rsquo;laimah be&rsquo;emes</span>] &mdash; for this world is entirely darkness [<span class="heb-term">tzail ovayr</span>], and the main purpose of true complete counsel is when one merits to succeed through his hand in the eternal world. And counsel of this sort &mdash; it is impossible to attain except through <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> [faith in the Sages] and drawing close to them and studying their holy books [<span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;faraihem</span>], which are full of true and deep counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzos amitiyos, aitzos amukkos</span>]. For also in the service of Hashem itself there are how many and how many counsels [<span class="heb-term">aitzos</span>] where the person is confused in them and turns them to evil &mdash; for the Torah contains two strengths [<span class="heb-term">koichos</span>], merit, etc., not merit, etc. &mdash; as is written: &ldquo;the righteous will walk in them and sinners will stumble in them.&rdquo; And therefore we need to serve many true Tzaddikim and holy faithful ones [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;shairim amitiyim</span>] in order to merit true complete counsel at every time and at every moment.</p>

<!-- OAS 2 -->
<div class="section-marker">2</div>

<p class="no-indent">For the main purpose of the <span class="concept">downfall began from evil counsels</span> [<span class="heb-term">aitzos ra&rsquo;os</span>], which are the <span class="concept">counsel of the Primordial Snake</span> [<span class="heb-term">Nachash haKadmoni</span>], in the aspect of the counsel of the Primeval Snake, etc. And from then the nation was corrupted, and the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> began from Avraham Avinu, from whom the drawing of the Torah into the world that is called &ldquo;counsel&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] began, as is written: &ldquo;I have counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] and sound wisdom [<span class="heb-term">tushiyah</span>]&rdquo; <span class="verse-source">(Mishlai 8:14)</span>. In the aspect of 613 counsels [<span class="heb-term">TaRYa&ldquo;G aitzin</span>], for Avraham merited that his tools [<span class="heb-term">kailav</span>] were springs [<span class="heb-term">nov&rsquo;os</span>] of wisdom, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said. &ldquo;His tools&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">kailav</span>] specifically, for <span class="heb-term">kli</span> [vessel] is &ldquo;counsel,&rdquo; and there the main point of the completeness of wisdom is found. When one merits through the wisdom to true counsel that will succeed through his hand &mdash; to escape the &ldquo;storm-wind&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">ru&rsquo;ach s&rsquo;arah</span>] of this world, and to succeed through one&rsquo;s hand forever. And therefore Avraham merited to be called a &ldquo;counselor&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">yo&rsquo;aitz</span>] to the Holy One, blessed is He, as is written: &ldquo;with whom He took counsel [<span class="heb-term">no&rsquo;atz</span>] and he will make him understand&rdquo; <span class="verse-source">(Y&rsquo;shayahu 40:14)</span>, etc. And is written: &ldquo;and the man of his counsel [<span class="heb-term">atzaso</span>] will make him know.&rdquo; This is stated about Avraham, as Rashi explains there. And so too, all the Tzaddikim are called &ldquo;counselors&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">yo&rsquo;atzim</span>], as is written: &ldquo;they were potters and dwellers of plantations [<span class="heb-term">n&rsquo;ta&rsquo;im</span>] with the King in His work.&rdquo; For in them is taking counsel [<span class="heb-term">nimlach</span>] and consulting [<span class="heb-term">nis&rsquo;ya&rsquo;aitz</span>] in the creation [<span class="heb-term">b&rsquo;riyah</span>] of worlds.</p>

<!-- OAS 3 -->
<div class="section-marker">3</div>

<p class="no-indent">And the main purpose of the Churban of the Bais HaMikdash and the exile of Yisrael from their land is the aspect of the <span class="concept">damage to the counsel</span> [<span class="heb-term">p&rsquo;gam ha&rsquo;aitzah</span>] that was divided into two &mdash; which came through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>, as above. For through this, Yisrael is driven from their land, as is explained there. And through this one cannot sweeten the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> [judgments] through <span class="heb-term">Kodesh Kodashim</span> [the Holy of Holies], and therefore through this the Bais HaMikdash was destroyed. And therefore we are established to fast the <span class="concept">four fasts</span> [<span class="heb-term">arba ta&rsquo;aniyos</span>] over this, in order to rectify through the fasts the damage of the foul smokes [<span class="heb-term">ashanos s&rsquo;ruchim</span>], which are the excesses [<span class="heb-term">mosros</span>] of eating that rise to the brain [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>] through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>.</p>

<!-- OAS 4 -->
<div class="section-marker">4</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">three calamities</span> [<span class="heb-term">sh&rsquo;losh tzaros</span>] that befell in the good [days] when the Churban of the Bais HaMikdash began, as is written: &ldquo;write for yourself this very day.&rdquo; And they are mentioned in the <span class="heb-term">S&rsquo;lichos</span> [penitential prayers] of Yom Kippur in the good [days] in which the Torah was written in Greek [<span class="heb-term">Yevanis</span>], and the <span class="heb-term">eizra hasofer</span> [Ezra the Scribe] died, and then <span class="heb-term">Samach Melech Bavel</span> [a king of Babylon came close], etc., which is the beginning of the Churban. For all these calamities are interdependent. For the Torah was written in Greek &mdash; this is the main point of the aspect of the damage to &ldquo;the writing of their hand&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;sav yadainu</span>], and an impairment requiring rectification so that their writing [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;sivah</span>] &mdash; since the holy Torah itself was written in their writing. And this is the aspect of the death of Ezra the Scribe &mdash; who was the foremost scribe, whose entire endeavor was to rectify the writing of the Torah as is fitting. And therefore the distress of his death is connected to the distress of the writing of the Torah in their writing &mdash; which is the opposite of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> that Ezra the Scribe worked through being occupied in being a scribe and writing in our writing as our law. And the continuation of the completeness of the writing of the books of the Torah in the world &mdash; and therefore the Churban began. For the main point of the Churban is through this &mdash; through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through which the &ldquo;writing of our hand&rdquo; is damaged and Yisrael are driven from Eretz Yisrael and the counsel is divided. And then there is no completeness for the Torah through damaging [<span class="heb-term">pogmim</span>] the true books [<span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;farim amitiyim</span>] of our holy Torah &mdash; for through this, one cannot draw the sweetening from Kodesh Kodashim. See there and see how all this is connected with this.</p>

<!-- OAS 5 -->
<div class="section-marker">5</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">division of the Sh&rsquo;vatim</span> [tribes] together with Yosef &mdash; the aspect of their exile and Churban &mdash; for Yosef is the aspect of the <span class="concept">Tzaddik of truth</span>. And the Sh&rsquo;vatim &mdash; even though they are all holy ones [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;doshim</span>] &mdash; even so, the Satan leaped between them and misled them with evil counsels [<span class="heb-term">aitzos ra&rsquo;os</span>], as if to recognize the Yosef of the true counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>]. For also great Tzaddikim need to guard themselves very much and to seek from Hashem, blessed be He, that He will always be blessed with them &mdash; to be saved from evil counsels [<span class="heb-term">aitzos ra&rsquo;os</span>], particularly in the matter of <span class="concept">machlokes</span> [strife] that places the <span class="concept">main root of the struggle between the Tzaddikim</span>, until it was shown to them [the Sh&rsquo;vatim] that they are thieves [<span class="heb-term">ganavim</span>] and deceivers [<span class="heb-term">ramaim</span>], <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> &mdash; as if all their conduct was robbery and deception, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> &mdash; and then the Sh&rsquo;vatim recognized the great damage, and how damage reaches through the Tzaddik of truth who damages through the damage of the true counsel of the Sages that are caused through this &mdash; specifically the counsel of the higher world [<span class="heb-term">seichel ha&rsquo;elyon</span>] as above. And the <span class="concept">Sh&rsquo;vatim returned in t&rsquo;shuvah in completeness</span>, and then were included together, and then Moshiach will come &mdash; the aspect of the final <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> at the end, when Moshiach comes &mdash; then the kingdom of the house of Dovid will be reunited, which was initially divided &mdash; the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the damage to the counsel as above &mdash; and they will no longer go out to two kingdoms [<span class="heb-term">malchuyos</span>] any more. For the division of the kingdom of the house of Dovid and the division of the counsel are one aspect (as is written elsewhere). And therefore they read the <span class="heb-term">Haftarah</span> of this in <span class="concept">Parashas VaYigash</span>, which speaks about the unification of the kingdoms of the house of Yisrael, as is written there; and they will no longer go out to two kingdoms any more, etc. And therefore it is called <span class="concept">Moshiach Peleh Yo&rsquo;aitz</span> [&ldquo;Wondrous Counselor&rdquo;]. And is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and upon him rests the spirit of Hashem, a spirit of wisdom and understanding, a spirit of counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] and might&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse-source">(Y&rsquo;shayahu 11:2)</span>. For the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> is the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel, which is the main purpose of the completeness [<span class="heb-term">sh&rsquo;laimus</span>] of the Torah, when one merits through the Tzaddik of truth to receive true counsel each and every one according to his aspect &mdash; in a way that he can save his soul from the pits of destruction [<span class="heb-term">min&rsquo;ai shachas</span>] and to merit through his hands the eternal salvation [<span class="heb-term">ha&rsquo;hatzalah ha&rsquo;nitzchis</span>].</p>

<!-- OAS 6 -->
<div class="section-marker">6</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore when the Sh&rsquo;vatim together with Yosef &mdash; it was impossible for Yosef to return and to rejoin with them until they brought <span class="concept">Binyamin</span> [Benjamin]. For Binyamin is the main focus of the aspect of the <span class="concept"><span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel</span>, the complete counsel &mdash; for it is only born in Eretz Yisrael, where the Bais HaMikdash stands &mdash; where the main focus of the counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] is, as above. And therefore it is called <span class="heb-term">Binyamin &mdash; Ben Yamim</span> [&ldquo;son of days&rdquo;], in the aspect of true counsel that is in the aspect of &ldquo;the heart of a wise man [<span class="heb-term">chacham</span>] to his right [<span class="heb-term">li&rsquo;mino</span>]&rdquo; &mdash; the very opposite of evil counsels which are in the aspect of &ldquo;the heart of a fool [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;sil</span>] to his left [<span class="heb-term">li&rsquo;s&rsquo;moilo</span>]&rdquo; &mdash; for the twelve [<span class="heb-term">Yud-Bais</span>] Sh&rsquo;vatim are the aspect of the complete counsel [<span class="heb-term">sh&rsquo;laimus</span>] of the totality of the holy counsel, which is the totality of the Torah called &ldquo;counsel&rdquo; as above. For the twelve Sh&rsquo;vatim are the aspect of the twelve sons [<span class="heb-term">Banei</span>] of Yaakov who are all included in one stone (as brought there in the Torah, as above; see there) &mdash; meaning, this is the aspect of what is included in the stone &mdash; it was the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Kodesh Kodashim</span> [the Holy of Holies] &mdash; which is attained through <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through which are composed the true books [<span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;farim</span>] of the holy Torah &mdash; for all of this is the aspect of the complete counsel of the holy counsel, which is the totality of the Torah called &ldquo;counsel,&rdquo; as above. For the twelve Sh&rsquo;vatim are the aspect of the twelve stones [<span class="heb-term">avanei</span>] of Yaakov that were all included in one stone (as brought there in the Torah, as above; see there) &mdash; that this is the aspect of what is included in the stone &mdash; it was the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Kodesh Kodashim</span>, which is attained through <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>. And therefore Yaakov was very weary when Yosef was born, to flee with his flocks outside the Land, as is written in the Zohar HaKadosh, that he is &ldquo;born from one from within another&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of the holy of the holiest [<span class="heb-term">kodesh k&rsquo;dashim</span>] &mdash; the aspect of the completeness of the holy Torah on Yaakov&rsquo;s behalf, as is written &ldquo;and He chose Yaakov for Himself.&rdquo; And therefore the completeness of the holy bed [<span class="heb-term">mitah sh&rsquo;laimah</span>] is completed through Binyamin, that the necessity is to be in Eretz Yisrael where the Bais HaMikdash and Kodesh Kodashim stand &mdash; where the main focus of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] is, as above.</p>

<!-- OAS 7 -->
<div class="section-marker">7</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore when the Sh&rsquo;vatim came to Mitzrayim and [Yosef] saw that they were returning in t&rsquo;shuvah over their selling of him, and yet still they needed to return and rejoin with him, and then it would be finished and complete [<span class="heb-term">nigmar v&rsquo;nishlam</span>] &mdash; the counsel &mdash; therefore he did not want to make himself known [<span class="heb-term">l&rsquo;hisvada</span>] to them until they would bring Binyamin. And also then he added to cause them pain, in order that they would return in complete t&rsquo;shuvah even more. And he would cause them pain through Binyamin specifically, so that they would feel through the truth what was impacted through the selling of Yosef the Tzaddik &mdash; which is the aspect of the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>, which was caused through this &mdash; the damage to the counsel as above. For the main point of the &ldquo;damage&rdquo; reaches Binyamin, the Tzaddik of truth, who comes to the completeness of the Torah through his holy teachings [<span class="heb-term">D&rsquo;rashos</span>], which are the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through the masters [<span class="heb-term">ribbuyai</span>] of the holy books of the Tzaddikim of truth &mdash; for through this, specifically, they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive [<span class="heb-term">seichel haKolail</span>] (see there) &mdash; through which all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> [judgments] are sweetened throughout the world. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">v&rsquo;nichsav baSeifer</span>], as said in the war of Amalek. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo; &mdash; meaning, the main purpose of the subduing of Haman-Amalek is through the masters of the holy books of the Torah &mdash; through which they are included in the intellect of the All-Inclusive and as above.</p>

<!-- OAS 8 -->
<div class="section-marker">8</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">fasts that are decreed over the rains</span> [<span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;aniyos she&rsquo;gozrim al ha&rsquo;g&rsquo;shamim</span>]. For the main point of the ceasing of rains [<span class="heb-term">atziras g&rsquo;shamim</span>] comes from the damage to emunah [faith], as is written: &ldquo;and you turned away and you served [idols]&rdquo;, etc., &ldquo;and He closed the heavens,&rdquo; etc. Meaning, through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>, which is the main point of the foundation [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;sod</span>] of the emunah, and therefore fasts are decreed &mdash; for through the fasts, the excess [<span class="heb-term">mosros</span>] of eating are rectified, which confuse the brain [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>], etc., as above, regarding the matter of the four fasts. For the fast is the aspect of t&rsquo;shuvah, and through this is drawn the aspect of <span class="heb-term">peleg Elokim malei mayim</span> [&ldquo;the stream of G-d is full of water&rdquo;] which brings the rains (as is explained in the Torah, as above; see there). And therefore the main purpose of the fasting over the rains is in Eretz Yisrael, where specifically all the thirteen fasts are decreed, corresponding to the <span class="concept">Sh&rsquo;losh Esreh M&rsquo;chilin D&rsquo;Rachamei</span> [thirteen implements of mercy] &mdash; through which the sweetening of all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> [judgments] &mdash; that the main point of which is rooted in the intellect of the higher world [<span class="heb-term">seichel ha&rsquo;elyon</span>] &mdash; in the aspect of the holiest holy ones [<span class="heb-term">kodshai k&rsquo;dashim</span>] &mdash; where the place of all the thirteen implements of mercy as is known. And from there are drawn the <span class="concept">thirty-two midos</span> [dimensions] of the Torah, which are taught in them &mdash; through which the main point of clarification of all the halachos of the Torah &mdash; which are the aspect of clarification of the holy counsel &mdash; for the halachos of the Torah are themselves the counsel, in the aspect of TaRYa&ldquo;G counsels [<span class="heb-term">aitzin</span>] of the Oral Torah [<span class="heb-term">D&rsquo;Oraisa</span>] &mdash; which are TaRYa&ldquo;G counsels that it is impossible to clarify all their laws and halachos except through the thirty-two midos by which the Torah is expounded [<span class="heb-term">nidreshes</span>] in them. And likewise regarding the matter of <span class="heb-term">avodah</span> [service] and the fulfillment of the Torah, we need to place counsel in our souls through the aspect of the thirteen midos by which the Torah is expounded in them (as is explained elsewhere). It emerges that the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel that comes through the sweetening of the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> through t&rsquo;shuvah over the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through this the Torah is made complete &mdash; through which one merits the intellect of the all-inclusive [<span class="heb-term">seichel ha&rsquo;kolail</span>] &mdash; where the sweetening of all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> is rooted &mdash; all of this is drawn through the <span class="concept">Sh&rsquo;losh Esreh M&rsquo;chilin D&rsquo;Rachamei</span>, which are the aspect of the thirty-two midos [of Torah exposition] &mdash; which are themselves the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel both for the <span class="heb-term">halachah</span> and for action &mdash; for the fulfillment of the Torah, as above. And therefore thirteen fasts are decreed, as above, for the fasts over the rains are for the purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel, which is drawn through the aspect of <span class="heb-term">peleg Elokim malei mayim</span> that brings the rains &mdash; which is the aspect of the water [<span class="heb-term">mayim</span>] that purifies from the filth [<span class="heb-term">tinofes</span>] and the foul smokes [<span class="heb-term">ashanos s&rsquo;ruchim</span>], as above, which come through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through which the counsel is damaged and divided (as all this is explained in the Torah, as above; see there, well).</p>

<!-- OAS 9 -->
<div class="section-marker">9</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the fasts that are decreed over the rains. For the main point of the ceasing of rains comes from the damage to emunah, as is written, etc. Meaning, through the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span>, which is the main point of the y&rsquo;sod of the emunah &mdash; and therefore fasts are decreed (as explained in the Torah, as above; see there).</p>

<!-- OAS 10 -->
<div class="section-marker">10</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">secret of the g&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah</span> [goblet] that is found in the truthfulness [<span class="heb-term">amitachus</span>] of Binyamin. For Binyamin is the main point of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the complete counsel [<span class="heb-term">sh&rsquo;laimus ha&rsquo;aitzah</span>], for it is only born in Eretz Yisrael &mdash; the Bais HaMikdash and Kodesh Kodashim &mdash; in their portions, etc. And there &mdash; the secret of the g&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah &mdash; which is the aspect of the completeness of the counsel drawn through t&rsquo;shuvah over the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through which the books of the Torah [<span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;farim</span>] are composed and the Torah is made complete, and it is included in the aspect of Kodesh Kodashim &mdash; where all the Sh&rsquo;losh Esreh M&rsquo;chilin D&rsquo;Rachamei reside &mdash; through which all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> are sweetened, etc., as above. For as it says in the Yerushalmi, the &ldquo;G&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah of depth&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">M&rsquo;gillah Amukkos</span>] &mdash; its g&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah is the aspect of thirteen parts [<span class="heb-term">P&rsquo;rakim</span>], 72 [letters], which are the letters of g&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah &mdash; which are the thirteen M&rsquo;chilin D&rsquo;Rachamei, meaning as above. And this is what is brought there, that the Yud-Bais times 72 of the above are in <span class="heb-term">gematria</span> &ldquo;complete&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">shalom</span>] in the Mem <span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;sumah</span> [closed final Mem], etc. See there. For the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> through <span class="heb-term">shalom</span> [peace] &mdash; which is the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> [strife/division] &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the damage to <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> (as is explained there in the Torah, as above and as above).</p>

<!-- OAS 11 -->
<div class="section-marker">11</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">twelve Sh&rsquo;vatim</span> who correspond to the <span class="concept">twelve months</span> [<span class="heb-term">Yud-Bais chodshim</span>], in the aspect of true counsel that is the aspect of &ldquo;the heart of a wise man to his right&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">lev chacham li&rsquo;mino</span>] &mdash; the very opposite of evil counsels which are in the aspect of &ldquo;the heart of a fool to his left&rdquo; &mdash; for the twelve Sh&rsquo;vatim are the aspect of the <span class="concept">complete counsel</span> of the holy counsel &mdash; the totality of the Torah &mdash; called &ldquo;counsel,&rdquo; as above. For they are the very bed of the completeness that Yaakov Avinu established, from whom all the seed of Yisrael went out, who received the Torah at Har Sinai, which is the main focus of the complete counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah sh&rsquo;laimah</span>], as above. For the twelve Sh&rsquo;vatim are the aspect of the twelve sons of Yaakov who are all included in one stone (as brought there in the Torah, as above; see there). This is the aspect of what is included in the stone &mdash; it was the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Kodesh Kodashim</span> &mdash; attained through <span class="heb-term">emunas Chachamim</span> &mdash; through which the true books of the Torah are composed &mdash; for all of this is the aspect of the complete counsel of the holy counsel that is completed through Binyamin &mdash; the need being to be in Eretz Yisrael where the Bais HaMikdash and Kodesh Kodashim stand &mdash; where the main focus of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] is, as above.</p>

<!-- OAS 12-15 -->
<div class="section-marker">12</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">machlokes between the Sh&rsquo;vatim</span> together with Yosef &mdash; the aspect of their exile and Churban &mdash; for Yosef is the aspect of the Tzaddik of truth. And the Sh&rsquo;vatim &mdash; even though they are all holy ones &mdash; even so, the Satan leaped between them and misled them with evil counsels, as if to recognize Yosef, the Tzaddik who damages through the damage of the true counsel of the Sages (as brought there in the Torah, as above; see there). That the main point of the &ldquo;damage&rdquo; reaches Binyamin, the Tzaddik of truth, who is more exalted even than the intellect of the all-inclusive as above &mdash; which is the aspect of Kodesh Kodashim &mdash; its preciousness being from the inside and from the inside &mdash; like the great honor that enters before him and before his face. And a Tzaddik such as this, in the aspect of Mordechai, can draw the sweetening from even the &ldquo;gate of the fifty&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">sha&rsquo;ar ha&rsquo;chamishim</span>] &mdash; from there &mdash; and to bring down Mordechai from the gate of the fifty of holiness [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;dushah</span>] and to hang himself there specifically (for when they cannot draw the sweetening from there, they can strengthen the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> even more, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>).</p>

<div class="section-marker">13</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore in truth there was a time of great distress, but Hashem, blessed be He, with abundant mercies reversed His counsel &mdash; for Mordechai had the power to ascend in Hashem&rsquo;s Name in the aspect of the higher world [<span class="heb-term">ha&rsquo;aliyah</span>] &mdash; for Mordechai is &ldquo;mar d&rsquo;ror&rdquo; [pure myrrh] &mdash; first in the heavens, which is the holiness of the Oil of Anointing [<span class="heb-term">Shemen HaMishchah</span>], from which is anointed the Mishkan and the vessels and Kodesh Kodashim. It emerges that the holiness of Kodesh Kodashim itself, and the holiness of the vessels &mdash; all is drawn from the Oil of Anointing, which is the aspect of the holiness of Mordechai, &ldquo;mar d&rsquo;ror.&rdquo; And this is the aspect of the great power of the Tzaddikim of truth, who are more exalted even than the intellect of the all-inclusive, as above &mdash; which is the aspect of Kodesh Kodashim. And a Tzaddik like this, in the aspect of Mordechai, can draw the sweetening from even the gate of the fifty, etc., as above. And therefore through Mordechai, all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> are sweetened through the aspect of the intellect of the higher world, as above &mdash; until he is turned from &ldquo;opposite to opposite,&rdquo; and his thoughts returned to him &ldquo;in his head&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">b&rsquo;rosho</span>], etc.</p>

<div class="section-marker">14</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">joy of Purim</span> [<span class="heb-term">simchas Purim</span>]. For when they are included together in the intellect of the higher world, as above, through this the main purpose of the <span class="concept">joy</span> [<span class="heb-term">simchah</span>] is in the aspect of the light of Tzaddikim that shines &mdash; as is explained there at the end of the Torah, as above &mdash; that this is the aspect of <span class="concept">&ldquo;Chadei Rabbi Shim&rsquo;on&rdquo;</span> [&ldquo;rejoice, Rabbi Shimon&rdquo;]; see there.</p>

<p>For Mordechai &mdash; this is [the one who was] open [<span class="heb-term">posai&rsquo;ach</span>] in words and teachings, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said &mdash; meaning, that he was the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through his holy teachings &mdash; that this is the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through the masters of the holy books of the Tzaddikim of truth &mdash; through which specifically they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive [<span class="heb-term">seichel ha&rsquo;kolail</span>] (see there) &mdash; through which all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> in the world are sweetened. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">v&rsquo;nichsav ba&rsquo;Seifer</span>] &mdash; that was said in the war of Amalek. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo; &mdash; meaning, the main purpose of the subduing of Haman-Amalek is through the masters of the holy books of the Torah &mdash; through which they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive and as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">15</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore it is advised [<span class="heb-term">nis&rsquo;ya&rsquo;aitz</span>] to make a <span class="concept">tree fifty cubits</span> [<span class="heb-term">aitz chamishim amah</span>] high to hang Mordechai &mdash; which is as against the gate of the fifty [<span class="heb-term">sha&rsquo;ar ha&rsquo;chamishim</span>], as is explained &mdash; which is the aspect of the intellect of the higher world of the all-inclusive that wants to bring down [<span class="heb-term">l&rsquo;hashlich</span>] Mordechai from there &mdash; which is the aspect of the hanging [<span class="heb-term">t&rsquo;liyah</span>]. For Elokim made this opposite this [<span class="heb-term">zeh l&rsquo;umas zeh</span>]. And the Haman wanted to strengthen himself in the intensity of the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span>, to receive power from the gate of the fifty of the <span class="heb-term">tumah</span> [impurity] and to bring down Mordechai specifically from the gate of the fifty of holiness (for when they cannot draw the sweetening from there, they can strengthen the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> even more, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>). And therefore through the strength and the might and the greatness of Mordechai the Tzaddik, who brought in the awakening of t&rsquo;shuvah so much in Yisrael &mdash; that they uprooted Yisrael to Hashem &mdash; the Name will be blessed in every heart until they merited wondrous and awesome miracles through this &mdash; to renew a holy book and awesome miracles like this &mdash; which is the <span class="concept">holy M&rsquo;gillah</span>, which is &ldquo;pirsumay nisa&rdquo; [publicizing of the miracle] &mdash; that its publication and revelation of its providence [<span class="heb-term">hashgachah</span>] will be blessed upon us at all times &mdash; even in the time of the <span class="heb-term">hester</span> [concealment] &mdash; for within the <span class="heb-term">hester</span>, which is the time of the intensity of the exile, in the sins of our many rabbis &mdash; even then He will be blessed beyond concealment, and He will be blessed &mdash; He Himself will hide, and He will attain us for our good, even in the time of the intensity of the distress, in wondrous and awesome ways, very, very much, that no creature can stand upon this. And through this He saves us from the angle of all our enemies and removes the counsel of our enemies in every generation and generation, as we saw then in the days of Mordechai and Esther &mdash; as is explained in the account of the holy M&rsquo;gillah &mdash; that we need to return hearts in simplicity to rectify the awesome trials [<span class="heb-term">nisyonos</span>] that the Name, blessed be He, made with us then. And likewise He conducts with us in mercy in every generation and generation.</p>

<!-- OAS 16-20 -->
<div class="section-marker">16</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">greatness of the mitzvah of reading the M&rsquo;gillah</span>. As Rabbainu, of blessed memory, noted in his exalted expression, that they annul the entire all-inclusive in the merit of its reading &mdash; as though the Kohanim are in their service and the L&rsquo;viyim on their platform, and Yisrael in their station &mdash; the all-inclusive nullifies the reading of the M&rsquo;gillah. And there is no mitzvah that is not pushed aside from before it, etc. For this is the main point of the wondrous novelty of Purim, which is greater than all the Festivals in this aspect, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said, that all the Festivals are nullified [<span class="heb-term">batailim</span>] and the days of Purim are not nullified. For we merited then through the strength and the might and the greatness of Mordechai the Tzaddik, who brought in the awakening of t&rsquo;shuvah so much in Yisrael that they uprooted to Hashem the Name &mdash; He will be blessed in every heart &mdash; until they merited to the wondrous miraculous revelation and awesome miracles, which is the holy M&rsquo;gillah, &ldquo;pirsumay nisa&rdquo; that publicizes and reveals His providence &mdash; He will be blessed upon us at all times &mdash; even in the time of the <span class="heb-term">hester</span>, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">17</div>

<p class="no-indent">For Mordechai &mdash; this is [the one who was] open [<span class="heb-term">posai&rsquo;ach</span>] in words and teachings, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said &mdash; meaning, that he was the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through his holy teachings &mdash; that this is the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through the masters of the holy books of the Tzaddikim of truth. Through which specifically they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive. See there &mdash; through which all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> in the world are sweetened. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;v&rsquo;nichsav baSeifer&rdquo; [&ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo;] that was said in the war of Amalek. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and it was written in the book&rdquo; &mdash; meaning, the main point of the subduing of Haman-Amalek is through the masters of the holy books of the Torah, through which they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive and as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">18</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore it is advised to make a tree fifty cubits [high] to hang Mordechai, which is as against the gate of the fifty, as above &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">seichel ha&rsquo;elyon</span> of the all-inclusive that wants to bring down Mordechai from there. And the Haman wanted to strengthen the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> in their intensity to receive power from the gate of the fifty of the <span class="heb-term">tumah</span> and to bring down Mordechai from the gate of the fifty of holiness &mdash; where the Kol [all-inclusive] enters, i.e. Kodesh Kodashim. And therefore they read the Haftarah of this in Parashas VaYigash, which speaks about the unification of the kingdoms of the house of Yisrael, and they will no longer go out to two kingdoms any more, etc. And therefore it is called Moshiach &ldquo;Peleh Yo&rsquo;aitz&rdquo; [Wondrous Counselor].</p>

<div class="section-marker">19</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore through Mordechai all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> are sweetened through the aspect of the intellect of the higher world as above, until he is turned from &ldquo;opposite to opposite&rdquo; and his thoughts returned to him &ldquo;in his head.&rdquo; For the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> is the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel which is the main point of the completeness of the Torah &mdash; when one merits through the Tzaddik of truth to receive true counsel, each and every one according to his aspect, in a way that he can save his soul from the pits of destruction, and merit through his hands the eternal salvation. And even though one hands over the choice [<span class="heb-term">b&rsquo;chirah</span>] to man &mdash; and therefore the necessity is to help the person that he should choose for himself counsel according to his will [<span class="heb-term">r&rsquo;tzono</span>] &mdash; even so &mdash; from Hashem, blessed be He, His counsel will always be done [<span class="heb-term">gumor tamid ki&rsquo;r&rsquo;tzono</span>]. (And see this elsewhere.) For the counsel [<span class="heb-term">aitzah</span>] of Hashem stands forever. And is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;for Hashem Tz&rsquo;vaos has counseled, and who shall annul it?&rdquo;</span></p>

<div class="section-marker">20</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">simchah of Purim</span>. For when they are included together in the intellect of the higher world, as above, through this the main purpose of the simchah is in the aspect of the light of the Tzaddikim that shines &mdash; as is explained there at the end of the Torah, as above &mdash; that this is the aspect of &ldquo;Chadei Rabbi Shim&rsquo;on&rdquo; [&ldquo;rejoice, Rabbi Shimon&rdquo;] &mdash; see there. That through Mordechai, specifically, this is the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through his holy teachings &mdash; that this is the aspect of the completeness of the Torah through the masters of the holy books of the Tzaddikim of truth &mdash; for through this, specifically, they are included in the intellect of the all-inclusive, as above &mdash; through which all the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> in the world are sweetened.</p>

<!-- OAS 21-26 -->
<div class="section-marker">21</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is also the aspect of the <span class="concept">greatness of the mitzvah of reading the M&rsquo;gillah</span>. As Rabbainu, of blessed memory, made wondrous in his exalted expression, that they annul the all-inclusive in the merit of its reading. As though the Kohanim were in their service and the L&rsquo;viyim on their platform, and Yisrael in their station &mdash; the all-inclusive nullifies in the merit of reading the M&rsquo;gillah. And there is no mitzvah that is not pushed aside from before it, etc. For this is the main point of the <span class="concept">wondrous novelty [<span class="heb-term">chiddush ha&rsquo;nifla</span>] of Purim</span>, which is greater than all the Festivals in this aspect, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said &mdash; that all the Festivals are nullified and the days of Purim are not nullified. For we merited then, through the strength and might and greatness of Mordechai the Tzaddik, who brought in the awakening of t&rsquo;shuvah so much in Yisrael &mdash; that they uprooted Yisrael to Hashem &mdash; He will be blessed in every heart &mdash; until they merited wondrous [revelations] and awesome miracles like this &mdash; which is the holy M&rsquo;gillah, which is &ldquo;pirsumay nisa&rdquo;; and that it publicizes and reveals His providence upon us at all times, even in the time of the <span class="heb-term">hester</span> &mdash; in the time of the intensity of the exile &mdash; in the sins of our many rabbis, even then He is blessed beyond concealment, and He Himself hides and attains us for our good, even in the time of the intensity of the distress in wondrous and awesome paths, very, very much, that no creature can stand upon this. And through this He saves us from the angle of all our enemies and reverses the counsel of our enemies in every generation and generation, as we saw then in the days of Mordechai and Esther.</p>

<div class="section-marker">22</div>

<p class="no-indent">As is explained in the account of the holy M&rsquo;gillah, that we need to return hearts in simplicity to rectify the awesome <span class="heb-term">nisyonos</span> [trials] that Hashem, blessed be He, made with us then. And likewise He conducts with us in mercy in every generation and generation.</p>

<div class="section-marker">23</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore the <span class="concept">Haftarah</span> of this is read in <span class="concept">Parashas VaYigash</span>, which speaks about the unification of the kingdoms of the house of Yisrael, as is written there &mdash; and they will no longer go out to two kingdoms any more, etc. And therefore it is called <span class="concept">Moshiach &ldquo;Peleh Yo&rsquo;aitz&rdquo;</span>. And is written: &ldquo;and upon him rests the spirit of Hashem, a spirit of wisdom and understanding, a spirit of counsel and might.&rdquo; For the main purpose of the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> is the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of the counsel, which is the main purpose of the completeness of the Torah &mdash; when one merits through the Tzaddik of truth to receive true counsel, each and every one according to his aspect, in a way that he can save his soul from the pits of destruction and merit through his hands the eternal salvation.</p>

<div class="section-marker">24</div>

<p class="no-indent">And even though one hands over the choice [<span class="heb-term">b&rsquo;chirah</span>] to man &mdash; and therefore the necessity is to help the person that he should choose for himself counsel according to his will &mdash; even so, from Hashem His counsel will always be as He wishes. (And see this elsewhere.) For the counsel of Hashem stands forever. And is written: &ldquo;for Hashem Tz&rsquo;vaos has counseled, and who shall annul it?&rdquo;</p>

<div class="section-marker">25</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore we fast over the ceasing of rains to rectify the <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> [strife] &mdash; meaning, the wars that cause the ceasing of rains, as above. And this is also the aspect of the <span class="concept">four fasts</span> that we fast over the Churban, which is also to <span class="concept">rectify the <span class="heb-term">shalom</span></span> [peace]. As Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said: when there is no <span class="heb-term">shalom</span>, fast! &mdash; for the main purpose of fasting is when there is no <span class="heb-term">shalom</span> (as is explained there in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, in siman 268 [of the above]). For Yerushalayim was not destroyed except on account of <span class="heb-term">sin&rsquo;as chinam</span> [baseless hatred], as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, said. And therefore we fast to rectify this &mdash; for through the fast, the <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> is rectified and <span class="heb-term">shalom</span> is made, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">26</div>

<p class="no-indent">And so too regarding every distress [<span class="heb-term">tzarah</span>] that must not come &mdash; we fast. For all the distresses and the sufferings [<span class="heb-term">yisurim</span>], <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, are the aspect of <span class="concept">machlokes</span> [strife]. For whatever is opposite [<span class="heb-term">kneged</span>] a person&rsquo;s will is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> (and as is explained there in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, as above). For the distresses, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, are through the strengthening [<span class="heb-term">hisgabrus</span>] of the <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> [judgments], <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>. For there are no sufferings without sin [<span class="heb-term">avon</span>] (Shabbas 55a), and the sin is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> &mdash; for the main suckling of the Sitra Achara and the yaitzer hara is from <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> (as is explained there in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, as above). It emerges that through the sins that damaged through <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> &mdash; that gave power, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, to the Sitra Achara, which prevails over the holiness &mdash; therefore <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> are aroused upon him, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> &mdash; and from there come the distresses, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> &mdash; which are as against one&rsquo;s will &mdash; the aspect of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>. And to <span class="concept">rectify this, fasting is decreed</span> &mdash; which is the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>, as above. For the general rule is that opposite every type of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>, the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> is fasting, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;marbeh tz&rsquo;dakah, marbeh shalom&rdquo;</span> [&ldquo;abundant charity, abundant peace&rdquo;]. And the main purpose of the fast is the <span class="heb-term">tz&rsquo;dakah</span> [charity/righteousness], for <span class="verse">&ldquo;agra d&rsquo;sa&rsquo;anisa tzidkasa&rdquo;</span> [&ldquo;the reward of a fast is the charity&rdquo;]; see there.</p>

<p class="blessed">Blessed is Hashem forever, Amain and Amain.</p>

